{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e5f8ef6593dcb73d","name":"card_event_decoy_tactics","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Finland/events/card_event_decoy_tactics","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DECOY TACTICS","text":"Give a unit Ambush, Shock and: \"Enemy discards a random card when they target or attack this unit.\"","flavorText":"In February 1944, the Soviet Union launched three large-scale bombing raids against Helsinki, aiming to cripple Finnish morale and force the country into abandoning its alliance with Germany. The raids, approved at the 1943 Tehran Conference with British and American support, targeted the Finnish capital on the nights of February 6-7, 16-17, and 26-27. Soviet air forces deployed over 2,100 bombers and dropped more than 16,000 bombs during these operations. Anticipating such attacks, Finnish defenses implemented a sophisticated deception strategy. Fires were set on outlying islands and searchlights were activated only east of the city to mislead Soviet pathfinder aircraft. These tactics convinced the Soviet crews that they were striking central Helsinki, while in reality most bombs fell outside the urban core. The result was remarkably effective. Only 530 bombs hit the city itself, causing significantly fewer casualties than similar raids elsewhere in Europe. Finland also spread disinformation via Swedish channels, falsely claiming Helsinki had been devastated. When Soviet officials visited after the war, they were stunned to find the city largely untouched. Stalin, furious at the failure and deception, dismissed Marshal Golovanov, commander of the Soviet Strategic Air Force.","faction":"Finland","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_decoy_tactics","title":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_decoy_tactics_title","SourceString":"DECOY TACTICS","LocalizedString":"DECOY TACTICS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Finland","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_decoy_tactics_text","SourceString":"Give a unit Ambush, Shock and: \"Enemy discards a random card when they target or attack this unit.\"","LocalizedString":"Give a unit Ambush, Shock and: \"Enemy discards a random card when they target or attack this unit.\""},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_decoy_tactics_history","SourceString":"In February 1944, the Soviet Union launched three large-scale bombing raids against Helsinki, aiming to cripple Finnish morale and force the country into abandoning its alliance with Germany. The raids, approved at the 1943 Tehran Conference with British and American support, targeted the Finnish capital on the nights of February 6-7, 16-17, and 26-27. Soviet air forces deployed over 2,100 bombers and dropped more than 16,000 bombs during these operations. Anticipating such attacks, Finnish defenses implemented a sophisticated deception strategy. Fires were set on outlying islands and searchlights were activated only east of the city to mislead Soviet pathfinder aircraft. These tactics convinced the Soviet crews that they were striking central Helsinki, while in reality most bombs fell outside the urban core. The result was remarkably effective. Only 530 bombs hit the city itself, causing significantly fewer casualties than similar raids elsewhere in Europe. Finland also spread disinformation via Swedish channels, falsely claiming Helsinki had been devastated. When Soviet officials visited after the war, they were stunned to find the city largely untouched. Stalin, furious at the failure and deception, dismissed Marshal Golovanov, commander of the Soviet Strategic Air Force.","LocalizedString":"In February 1944, the Soviet Union launched three large-scale bombing raids against Helsinki, aiming to cripple Finnish morale and force the country into abandoning its alliance with Germany. The raids, approved at the 1943 Tehran Conference with British and American support, targeted the Finnish capital on the nights of February 6-7, 16-17, and 26-27. Soviet air forces deployed over 2,100 bombers and dropped more than 16,000 bombs during these operations. Anticipating such attacks, Finnish defenses implemented a sophisticated deception strategy. Fires were set on outlying islands and searchlights were activated only east of the city to mislead Soviet pathfinder aircraft. These tactics convinced the Soviet crews that they were striking central Helsinki, while in reality most bombs fell outside the urban core. The result was remarkably effective. Only 530 bombs hit the city itself, causing significantly fewer casualties than similar raids elsewhere in Europe. Finland also spread disinformation via Swedish channels, falsely claiming Helsinki had been devastated. When Soviet officials visited after the war, they were stunned to find the city largely untouched. Stalin, furious at the failure and deception, dismissed Marshal Golovanov, commander of the Soviet Strategic Air Force."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSuppressed","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardAttacks","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardRetreat"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Finland/10_Homefront/T_decoy_tactics.T_decoy_tactics","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/DECOY_TACTICS.DECOY_TACTICS","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":309.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_decoy_tactics_photo","SourceString":"Destruction from the bombing of Helsinki on the night of February 6 to 7, 1944.","LocalizedString":"Destruction from the bombing of Helsinki on the night of February 6 to 7, 1944."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[{"name":"ShouldDiscard","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"TargetedUnitRetreated","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_decoy_tactics_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsUnit_isIt","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"body":[{"op":"Context","at":0,"object":{"op":"Variable","name":"cardFunction","type":"ACardFunctionsStub*","scope":"member","sourceOp":"InstanceVariable"},"value":{"op":"LocalVirtualFunction","name":"GetTargetedCard","signature":"CardFunctionsStub.GetTargetedCard","args":[{"op":"Self"},{"op":"Variable","name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","scope":"local","sourceOp":"LocalVariable"},{"op":"Variable","name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"UBaseCardObject*","scope":"local","sourceOp":"LocalVariable"}]}},{"op":"JumpIfNot","at":55,"to":219,"condition":{"op":"Variable","name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","scope":"local","sourceOp":"LocalVariable"}},{"op":"Context","at":69,"object":{"op":"Variable","name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"